                                  GIT & GITHUB
             ----------------------------------------------------------


Git - Git id Distributed Version Control System
    - Version control means keeping track of changes made to project
    - Track changes in the code
    - Save different versions of the code
    - Working with other developers  
    - Restore old versions if something goes wrong


Respiratory - It is simply a project folder that Git manages
Commit - It is a saved snapshot of your project at a specific point of time
Github - It is a cloud platform that stores git respitories online,where git projects are stored, shared and collaberated on


     GIT Commands
    -----------------

    git --version - check if git is installed
    git init - ti initialize a new git repository'
    git status - show the current status of the repository
    git add . - stage all changes
    git commit - m "message"- save a snapshot of staged changes
    {
        git remote add origin url - Link a local repository to Github
        git push - u origin main - upload code to github and set upstream

    }
    Git push - Upload new commits
    Git pull - Download and merge changes from github
    Git clone <url> - copy a remote repository to your computer

 




 